{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery","id":359022,"title":"can splats learn sorcery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T05:41:16-08:00","id":359022,"title":"can splats learn sorcery?","content":"i think i read in a werewolf book that fera can and that some breeds even make a habit of doing so , vampires obviously can even if it works a bit differently and is stronger/ i also know that revenants can do it and some even become true mages<br /> what about changelings,wraiths kuei jin etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T06:53:48-08:00","id":359085,"title":"","content":"Half-splats, Ghouls/Kinfolk/Kinain/etc, usually can as can some Fera, notably Bastet and Kitsune are known for it (although I do seem to remember it as specifically mentioned ST fiat even for them), and it's debatable if Uktena dabble in it occasionally.<br /> <br /> Mostly the major splats, aside from the Changers that have a kind of ST fiat to being able to practice it as mentioned above, cannot use Hedge Magic and the old WoD: Sorcerer even had as an optional rule suggestions as to what kind of powers the newly Awakened/Embraced/etc. ex-Sorcerer might develop with a discount and faster learning, or even for free, according to his previous knowledge of Hedge Magic Paths.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised is kinda on the edge on whether or not they would retain their Paths despite Awakening but I cannot outright recall what the verdict was, though I myself would rather not allow one to mix True Magick, and yes I spelled it with the infamous k, with Hedge Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:22:18-08:00","id":359104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery#post359022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think i read in a werewolf book that fera can and that some breeds even make a habit of doing so , vampires obviously can even if it works a bit differently and is stronger/ i also know that revenants can do it and some even become true mages<br /> what about changelings,wraiths kuei jin etc?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a 7 point merit that allows Fera to buy Paths. If you feel other groups should have access to this I would apply this to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:35:45-08:00","id":359115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=359104#post359104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's a 7 point merit that allows Fera to buy Paths. If you feel other groups should have access to this I would apply this to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice catch I had forgotten that W20 locked it behind the Merit Cat/Fox Magic 7-pt's which allows one access to Hedge Magic Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T11:11:12-08:00","id":359327,"title":"","content":"There is a merit in a VtDA supplement called Wolves of the Sea (supplement about Viking Vampires) that allows you to purchase and use Sorcery Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T16:23:14-08:00","id":359647,"title":"","content":"Theoretically anyone can learn hedge magic except awakened mages, it's never outright stated that other supernaturals can't use it<br /> <br /> there's reason however, to say that the supernaturals in question would not be able to learn hedge magic and would instead learn other powers which come more naturally to them in the attempt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T22:59:57-08:00","id":359911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=359647#post359647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically anyone can learn hedge magic except awakened mages, it's never outright stated that other supernaturals can't use it</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. It *is* stressed, in several places, that hedge magic is very rare among non-Sorcerer splats; even before the 20 anniversary titles, it was easily understood to be something that would require a [M]erit akin to True Faith in order to have/use (with 20 later directly stating it that way as a 7pt. Merit). Also, it was directly stated that vampires could *never* use the hedge magic of mortals, directly (just as they can never work True Magic); they had to bastardize such magic into their own form of blood magic, via Thaumaturgy, Koldunism, what-have-you, as the ways in which mortals (Mage or Sorcerer, or merely gifted with a particular Numina) work magic is very different from how *they* must work it (via tapping into their own vitae to fuel &quot;x&quot; mystical effect). Your point stands in the broad, though -- it just should be qualified with how comparatively rare such things are (though you did mention how it's simply easier for &quot;x&quot; to develop Gifts/what-have-you, vs. mystical paths that are comparatively harder to attain).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:30:31-08:00","id":360163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=359911#post359911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly. It *is* stressed, in several places, that hedge magic is very rare among non-Sorcerer splats; even before the 20 anniversary titles, it was easily understood to be something that would require a [M]erit akin to True Faith in order to have/use (with 20 later directly stating it that way as a 7pt. Merit). Also, it was directly stated that vampires could *never* use the hedge magic of mortals, directly (just as they can never work True Magic); they had to bastardize such magic into their own form of blood magic, via Thaumaturgy, Koldunism, what-have-you, as the ways in which mortals (Mage or Sorcerer, or merely gifted with a particular Numina) work magic is very different from how *they* must work it (via tapping into their own vitae to fuel &quot;x&quot; mystical effect). Your point stands in the broad, though -- it just should be qualified with how comparatively rare such things are (though you did mention how it's simply easier for &quot;x&quot; to develop Gifts/what-have-you, vs. mystical paths that are comparatively harder to attain).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this begs the questio: how do sorcerers use their magic?? i mean mages avatars allow them to interact with the universe/magic/9 spheres etc . vampires blood magestwist the curse of cain. thus their power comes either entirely or mostly from within, even during rituals . <br /> <br /> how do sorcerers access their powers? especially werewolves and changelings which as i understand do not have avatars. and are not even really humans.. hell a wraith is more human than they are and yet they can' t learn sorcery!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:38:14-08:00","id":360169,"title":"","content":"Numina/Hedge Magic is based on folklore and ritual rituals passes down though the generations. <br /> <br /> Technically, anyone who has access to the right resources could learn it...you don't need to be endowed to do so. But, finding the right resources and having the right mind set to learn it, that's the tricky part and why it is a 7 points Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:01:22-08:00","id":360187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360169#post360169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Numina/Hedge Magic is based on folklore and ritual rituals passes down though the generations.<br /> <br /> Technically, anyone who has access to the right resources could learn it...you don't need to be endowed to do so. But, finding the right resources and having the right mind set to learn it, that's the tricky part and why it is a 7 points Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>my question was more like. how is sorcery powered? after all an intelligent robot doing it wouldachieve nothing<br /> where is that 7th point merit by the way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:55:25-08:00","id":360207,"title":"","content":"It's powered by Faith and Belief iirc.<br /> <br /> That merit was availabke to ghoul, kinfolk, kithain, and other mortal. I dont recall if it was in the original book if sorcery or part of the Kinfolk, ghoul and other &quot;Year of Ally&quot; books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T09:18:02-08:00","id":360238,"title":"","content":"What powers Numina (besides True Faith which is powered by faith) has always been left as something of an unanswered mystery. This allows Numina to be moved between the games and lets each splat have their own ideas about how/why it works (and only seems to work for things that are mostly human metaphysically) without one being secretly right the whole time. There are lots of answers in the books on what different groups think empowers Numina, but Numina don't really work well as a cross-game mechanic if they're only capable of being explained by one splat's metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:01:51-08:00","id":360401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360187#post360187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my question was more like. how is sorcery powered? after all an intelligent robot doing it wouldachieve nothing<br /> where is that 7th point merit by the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Citing this quote, but addressing your other post, as well...)<br /> <br /> Sorcerers' powers work because they are accessing the remaining power/belief (&quot;The Mythic Threads&quot;) that still exist in the world; they don't have to have Avatars to do that, as True Magic(k) -- even if a given Mage uses similar tools/methodologies as a given Sorcerer -- operates on a completely different metaphysical principle from Sorcery/Static Numina. It's also the reason why Sorcery doesn't normally create Paradox: whereas True Magic(k) alters Reality(tm) in order to make things happen, Sorcery works with the remaining threads of mysticism that are &quot;accepted&quot; by Reality(tm), and therefore don't disrupt it as greatly. (On the flip, however, as cited in Sorcerer, that is also why if in a situation where a Sorcerer's magic directly and incontrovertibly conflicts with Reality(tm) -- he casts a blatant fireball in a packed mall, surrounded by people, with the local news cameras on him, and it clearly is &quot;I'm casting a Fireball, bitches -- make your Reflex Saving Throws(tm)!&quot; -- then the spell will simply fail, as static magic *cannot*, by inherent definition, defy Reality(tm) on its face; a Mage, on the other hand, *could* accomplish the same feat -- though likely with Quintessence and Willpower to back it -- *BUT* would accrue Paradox for doing so... racking it up quite quickly with repeated castings, and absolutely having said Paradox come crashing down in short-order, Willpower or no Willpower, Teflon Avatar Merit or not...). Sidenote: the difference in metaphysical &quot;oomph&quot; also becomes clearer when the &quot;juice-stats&quot; are compared: Sorcerers generally can't have more than 5pts of Mana at any given time (assuming they have the appropriate Background), while even the lowliest Mage (unless using the DA:M alternative for Avatar/Fount, Quintessence scaling, which I strongly recommend as it better reflects the idea of the &quot;strength of the soul&quot;, and scales better relative to certain other splats) can have up to 20pts of Quintessence, due to his Awakened god-self.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> It's a 7pt merit in WW20 -- it allows (usually Kitsune or Bastet, though it could be anybody, theoretically) for the changer to be able to develop/practice static/hedge magic. (That puts in on a &quot;rarity scale&quot; similar to having True Faith, which is also 7pts.) I remember saying that, exactly, back in the 90's, as an appropriate Merit-cost for, say, the Uktena, or similar changers who might practice hedge magic (including the Ananasi, or of course the Kitsune). I remember getting the brush off by other posters, too. My response: White Wolf will figure it out one of these days...<br /> <br /> ... and it looks like my patience paid off... eventually... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:22:40-08:00","id":360516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360401#post360401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Citing this quote, but addressing your other post, as well...)<br /> <br /> Sorcerers' powers work because they are accessing the remaining power/belief (&quot;The Mythic Threads&quot;) that still exist in the world; they don't have to have Avatars to do that, as True Magic(k) -- even if a given Mage uses similar tools/methodologies as a given Sorcerer -- operates on a completely different metaphysical principle from Sorcery/Static Numina. It's also the reason why Sorcery doesn't normally create Paradox: whereas True Magic(k) alters Reality(tm) in order to make things happen, Sorcery works with the remaining threads of mysticism that are &quot;accepted&quot; by Reality(tm), and therefore don't disrupt it as greatly. (On the flip, however, as cited in Sorcerer, that is also why if in a situation where a Sorcerer's magic directly and incontrovertibly conflicts with Reality(tm) -- he casts a blatant fireball in a packed mall, surrounded by people, with the local news cameras on him, and it clearly is &quot;I'm casting a Fireball, bitches -- make your Reflex Saving Throws(tm)!&quot; -- then the spell will simply fail, as static magic *cannot*, by inherent definition, defy Reality(tm) on its face; a Mage, on the other hand, *could* accomplish the same feat -- though likely with Quintessence and Willpower to back it -- *BUT* would accrue Paradox for doing so... racking it up quite quickly with repeated castings, and absolutely having said Paradox come crashing down in short-order, Willpower or no Willpower, Teflon Avatar Merit or not...). Sidenote: the difference in metaphysical &quot;oomph&quot; also becomes clearer when the &quot;juice-stats&quot; are compared: Sorcerers generally can't have more than 5pts of Mana at any given time (assuming they have the appropriate Background), while even the lowliest Mage (unless using the DA:M alternative for Avatar/Fount, Quintessence scaling, which I strongly recommend as it better reflects the idea of the &quot;strength of the soul&quot;, and scales better relative to certain other splats) can have up to 20pts of Quintessence, due to his Awakened god-self.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> It's a 7pt merit in WW20 -- it allows (usually Kitsune or Bastet, though it could be anybody, theoretically) for the changer to be able to develop/practice static/hedge magic. (That puts in on a &quot;rarity scale&quot; similar to having True Faith, which is also 7pts.) I remember saying that, exactly, back in the 90's, as an appropriate Merit-cost for, say, the Uktena, or similar changers who might practice hedge magic (including the Ananasi, or of course the Kitsune). I remember getting the brush off by other posters, too. My response: White Wolf will figure it out one of these days...<br /> <br /> ... and it looks like my patience paid off... eventually... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> this does not explain sorcerers who operate on a scientific paradigm however.and correct me if im wrong it implies that if said belief dies off completely then sorcery will cease to exist. at least on earth? <br /> <br /> also since despire the fact that vampires and changelings could also never work the true magic of humans how comes they can learn it while vamps and wraiths are completely incapable?<br /> for vamps the only answer that i just came up with is that they can! learn it BUT their curse inherently empowers it.. for instance they would never need to spend one turn per level of the path they use, their difficulty numbers would be lower their rituals would be mostly independent free of the paths.,they would be consensus free etc. <br /> <br /> either that or they could learn it normally but eventually they would manage to &quot;upgrade&quot; it once they knew that they can power it with the power of their curse presumably the curse of caine has more &quot;juice&quot; than a changeling or fera does. either that or it's easier to &quot;bend&quot;(talk about god being drunk that day)<br /> <br /> the only difference seems to thatpaths go up to level 6<br /> after all now that i think of it, does sorcery really have any other advantage over thaumaturgy?(other than the fact that certain of it's ritualsare a bit..bloody talk about bad resonance lol)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:32:01-08:00","id":360526,"title":"","content":"@Mark,<br /> Only humans, some Bastet/Kitsune can learn Numina...maybe Garou.<br /> <br /> Vampire can only do blood magic and any numina becomes a corresponding path/Discipline,<br /> In thecase of wraith it becomes a corresponding Arcanoi.<br /> In the case of changeling a corresponding Glamour.<br /> <br /> In the Case of Opheus and Hunter, I'm not sure if they can learn Numica or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum