 that is also why if in a situation where a Sorcerer's magic directly and incontrovertibly conflicts with Reality(tm) -- he casts a blatant fireball in a packed mall, surrounded by people, with the local news cameras on him, and it clearly is &quot;I'm casting a Fireball, bitches -- make your Reflex Saving Throws(tm)!&quot; -- then the spell will simply fail, as static magic *cannot*, by inherent definition, defy Reality(tm) on its face; a Mage, on the other hand, *could* accomplish the same feat -- though likely with Quintessence and Willpower to back it -- *BUT* would accrue Paradox for doing so... racking it up quite quickly with repeated castings, and absolutely having said Paradox come crashing down in short-order, Willpower or no Willpower, Teflon Avatar Merit or not...). Sidenote: the difference in metaphysical &quot;oomph&quot; also becomes clearer when the &quot;juice-stats&quot; are compared: Sorcerers generally can't have more than 5pts of Mana at any given time (assuming they have the appropriate Background), while even the lowliest Mage (unless using the DA:M alternative for Avatar/Fount, Quintessence scaling, which I strongly recommend as it better reflects the idea of the &quot;strength of the soul&quot;, and scales better relative to certain other splats) can have up to 20pts of Quintessence, due to his Awakened god-self.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> It's a 7pt merit in WW20 -- it allows (usually Kitsune or Bastet, though it could be anybody, theoretically) for the changer to be able to develop/practice static/hedge magic. (That puts in on a &quot;rarity scale&quot; similar to having True Faith, which is also 7pts.) I remember saying that, exactly, back in the 90's, as an appropriate Merit-cost for, say, the Uktena, or similar changers who might practice hedge magic (including the Ananasi, or of course the Kitsune). I remember getting the brush off by other posters, too. My response: White Wolf will figure it out one of these days...<br /> <br /> ... and it looks like my patience paid off... eventually... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Careful my friend, whitewolf may go back on it's words sooner than later, you may be eating your words if they decide to change the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:15:36-08:00","id":360593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=359911#post359911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly. It *is* stressed, in several places, that hedge magic is very rare among non-Sorcerer splats; even before the 20 anniversary titles, it was easily understood to be something that would require a [M]erit akin to True Faith in order to have/use (with 20 later directly stating it that way as a 7pt. Merit). Also, it was directly stated that vampires could *never* use the hedge magic of mortals, directly (just as they can never work True Magic); they had to bastardize such magic into their own form of blood magic, via Thaumaturgy, Koldunism, what-have-you, as the ways in which mortals (Mage or Sorcerer, or merely gifted with a particular Numina) work magic is very different from how *they* must work it (via tapping into their own vitae to fuel &quot;x&quot; mystical effect). Your point stands in the broad, though -- it just should be qualified with how comparatively rare such things are (though you did mention how it's simply easier for &quot;x&quot; to develop Gifts/what-have-you, vs. mystical paths that are comparatively harder to attain).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> fair point, personally I think whitewolf fucked up on this and that the rule has no value, period. Hedge magic is a Mage based phenomenon and it's explanation in Mage does not allow for it's interpretation as being impossible to perform by Vampire's, that's a Vampire perspective on things, just like how &quot;Mages don't exist because they're extinct now&quot; is a Vampire perspective and one which was written in Tremere revised no less (a book which was published after Blood Treachery was, meaning that the Tremere were in conflict with the Order of Hermes at the time of writing).<br /> <br /> With these sorts of inconsistencies, one should question the application of outside material into another world of darkness game, including Sorcery being used in non Mage games and Sorcery being not useable in other games.<br /> <br /> My personal perspective: if a sleeper can do it, so can anyone else.<br /> <br /> I respect your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","user":"Dream_Walker","date":". 01-05-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:20:50-08:00","id":360597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360579#post360579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is this ever explicitly stated in any of the books?<br /> <br /> If so, where?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it was.<br /> <br /> 1) WOD: Sorceror p 54 and 55 (There they explicitely state on p 55 that a Sorceror cannot be a Changing Breed or Changeling, but can be related to one (Kinfolk, Enchanted human, etc.)<br /> <br /> 2) M:TA Sorceror Revised pp117-121.<br /> <br /> 3) W:TA Bastet (Qualmi only IIRC) and Hengeyokai (Kitsune only) Breed book state that these Changing breed can -with ST permission- learn Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 01-05-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:48:36-08:00","id":360626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360597#post360597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes it was.<br /> <br /> 1) WOD: Sorceror p 54 and 55 (There they explicitely state on p 55 that a Sorceror cannot be a Changing Breed or Changeling, but can be related to one (Kinfolk, Enchanted human, etc.)<br /> <br /> 2) M:TA Sorceror Revised pp117-121.<br /> <br /> 3) W:TA Bastet (Qualmi only IIRC) and Hengeyokai (Kitsune only) Breed book state that these Changing breed can -with ST permission- learn Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i could swear i saw some book that allowed changelings tobe sorcerers.. could be wrong though what's so special about these 2 changing breeds anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T15:00:40-08:00","id":360637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360626#post360626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i could swear i saw some book that allowed changelings tobe sorcerers.. could be wrong though what's so special about these 2 changing breeds anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be a book somewhere that allows Changeling to become Sorcerer...I must admit, it's not the Setting I'm most well-versed in.<br /> <br /> For the 2 Changing Breeds, it could just be thematically (or to take into account RL Legends/Depiction of cats and fox) but:<br /> In the case of Bastet, it's the way they are described as obsessed with Knowledge and secret as well as being great Magician.<br /> In the case of Kitsune, they are described as crafty and that they were able to get a lot of Gifts -including being able to do Hedge Magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T16:14:46-08:00","id":360731,"title":"","content":"Uktena have a Camp that traditionally learns it called Path Dancers, I think. Mokole in 1e were also presented as learning it, specifically, it seems, for the point of having voodou weregators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360593#post360593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> fair point, personally I think whitewolf fucked up on this and that the rule has no value, period. Hedge magic is a Mage based phenomenon and it's explanation in Mage does not allow for it's interpretation as being impossible to perform by Vampire's, that's a Vampire perspective on things, just like how &quot;Mages don't exist because they're extinct now&quot; is a Vampire perspective and one which was written in Tremere revised no less (a book which was published after Blood Treachery was, meaning that the Tremere were in conflict with the Order of Hermes at the time of writing).<br /> <br /> With these sorts of inconsistencies, one should question the application of outside material into another world of darkness game, including Sorcery being used in non Mage games and Sorcery being not useable in other games.<br /> <br /> My personal perspective: if a sleeper can do it, so can anyone else.<br /> <br /> I respect your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, hedge magic was originally detailed in Hunter's Hunted, so it's not really Mage-based. Mage just snapped it up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:30:09-08:00","id":360995,"title":"","content":"Regarding Changeling there might be some confusion due to terms used. Changeling can be a Sorcerer but that has nothing to do with Hedge Magic or mortal Sorcerers. Changeling Sorcerer is a Changeling with a considerable amount of Cantrips learned, I think, and this is straight out of memory ergo likely wrong, it was something on the line of having to have one set of Cantrips at level 5 and few others at level 4 to be considered Sorcerer the specifics escape me at the moment but they were rigorous demands that take a huge amount of exp to get if talking about a player.<br /> <br /> But no a Changeling is never gonna be using Hedge Magic they do not even have a merit for it unlike the Changers, the aforementioned Cat/Fox Magic 7-pts, or Vampires, in Wolves of the Sea (as mentioned by someone else) there is a 5pt Merits that allows them to have access to certain Paths of Hedge Magic but only certain Paths. So clearly it is meant to be something generally out of reach of Major Splats outside of expensive Merits that can grant access to them, the cost does not include the cost of the Path itself naturally thus keeping these to the truly dedicated few.<br /> <br /> Also WoD: Sorcerer as mentioned lays it out pretty straight saying that you loose your Hedge Magics should you become one of hte big splats but as an optional rule it gives you a list of what powers etc you might gain instead of your Path knowledge if and only if the ST is lenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T23:14:58-08:00","id":361032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360626#post360626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">i could swear i saw some book that allowed changelings tobe sorcerers.. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That'd be news to me. The magic of Changelings/The Fae is almost (not quite, but almost) diametrically opposite to how most sorcerer paths work/are structured, at least metaphysically speaking. Changelings' magic is much more dynamic, with certain metaphysical structures shifting even from one moment to the next; Sorcerers' magic is much more hardlined and patterned, relatively speaking, even if it does have *some* qualities of flexibility/versatility. The only thing more opposite to Fae magic is Vampiric Thaumaturgy (and their Disciplines, in general). I am not a complete expert on Changeling, but I've at least skimmed through almost all the books, and if I had ever read *anything* that said that, I'd have been all over it back in the day, because it's not metaphysically sound, at all. (Now, some fae-blooded individuals can certainly be Sorcerers -- I'm running a DA game for such a character right now -- and maybe that's what you're thinking of. Mages can be fae-blooded, too, though it's rare to the point of being unheard of in the Modern Era, and even rare during the Sorcerers Crusade and Dark Ages, though the Merit is available for mages back then. &gt;shrugs&lt; )</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360583#post360583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Careful my friend, whitewolf may go back on it's words sooner than later, you may be eating your words if they decide to change the rules.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nah. White Wolf's Common Sense Merit has finally (belatedly, but finally) kicked in for them... a couple decades late, perhaps, but &quot;better late than pregnant&quot;, as the old saying goes... </span></span></span><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360593#post360593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My personal perspective: if a sleeper can do it, so can anyone else.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But Sorcerers aren't Sleepers -- *that's the point*. They're not Awakened the way Mages are, but then neither are Vampires, or Garou, or Changelings/Fae, et al... Sorcerers aren't sleepers: their dedication and/or natural bend towards the mystical eventually manifests via their acquired mystical skills/powers (which can include Psychic Numina in some rare individuals, too). Sleepers *can't* work Path Magic without becoming Sorcerers, and very few humans/mortals have what it takes to become such (that's addressed in the books, as well). Any *given* individual might be able to become one, but on the whole few people have the drive/insight to make the leap. (Hell, that's why there's even a &quot;Sleep Walker&quot; Merit for Sorcerers -- it allows them to be &quot;awake&quot; enough to work *their* brand of juju, but still count as a Sleeper vs. *other* peoples' voodoo... there's a merit for that because </span></span></span><i>they're not Sleepers</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.) Just saying...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360731#post360731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, hedge magic was originally detailed in Hunter's Hunted, so it's not really Mage-based. Mage just snapped it up later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Even then, it was stated that vampires couldn't use mortal Hedge Magic, but had to use their own blood-fueled Disciplines and Thaumaturgy. Mage simply followed through on that (correct) metaphysical line of thinking (though, due to error in term-usage, some people got very confused about the differences between Hedge Magic and Awakened Magic(k), in 1st Ed. Mage; fortunately, they cleaned that up in 2nd Ed. and between Sorcerer to Sorcerer:Rev.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T05:51:17-08:00","id":361185,"title":"","content":"quoting frome werewolf storyteller's hand book revised.<br /> &quot;they don't possess individual avatars as mages know them (then it goes on about why they can' t be full mages)<br /> and the it says &quot;some rare shapeshifters are able to learn certain paths of hedge magic. sphere's magic's poor cousin. however it's hardly common practice whenall''s said and done the shapeshifters gifts and rites are at least as potent if not more so only the most curious or completist of the changing breeds feel the need to learn such human wizardry<br /> <br /> this seems to imply that other splats who have innate powers should be able to use sorcery. after all they to have some &quot;power&quot; they can bend right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 01-06-2015, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T07:11:51-08:00","id":362396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360516#post360516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this does not explain sorcerers who operate on a scientific paradigm however.and correct me if im wrong it implies that if said belief dies off completely then sorcery will cease to exist. at least on earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? If Sorcery works by exploiting elements of reality that can't (won't?) be changed, then it can't be eliminated. If it works based on the current universal paradigm (including the leftover bits from the old paradigms), then certain paths could wax, wane, disappear entirely, or new paths pop into existence.<br /> <br /> The new set of Revised Technocracy books (the ones that were released last year) suggest Enlightened Citizens (the Technocracy term for allied Sleepwalkers and Sorcerers) are on the rise. This would suggest that the scientific paradigm is becoming strong enough to support &quot;mythic threads&quot; of its own. Pure speculation on my part, but it seems to fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360526#post360526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Case of Opheus and Hunter, I'm not sure if they can learn Numica or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Orpheus (weren't the PCs in that normal people/occultists/scientists? Sounds like sorcery candidates to me), but the Imbued a.k.a &quot;Hunters&quot; cannot learn Sorcery or Numina (ST companion has a sidebar about why True Faith is not an option), and anyone who has Sorcery or Numina (including psychic powers) cannot be Imbued as a Hunter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=361185#post361185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and then it says &quot;some rare shapeshifters are able to learn certain paths of hedge magic. sphere's magic's poor cousin. however it's hardly common practice whenall's said and done the shapeshifters gifts and rites are at least as potent if not more so only the most curious or completist of the changing breeds feel the need to learn such human wizardry&quot;<br /> <br /> this seems to imply that other splats who have innate powers should be able to use sorcery. after all they to have some &quot;power&quot; they can bend right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. CWoD Sorcery is not like Exalted's thaumaturgy, where any being with knowledge and magical fuel can make use of it. Not every splat or character in the CWoD is going to have the metaphysical underpinnings to use it. Just because a splat has a source of supernatural power, that does not guarantee that they can manipulate their power (like the Tremere did to obtain Blood Magic), or that their power is even compatible with Sorcery (such as with the Imbued a.k.a. &quot;Hunters&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:51:45-08:00","id":362687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=361185#post361185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">quoting frome werewolf storyteller's hand book revised.<br /> &quot;they don't possess individual avatars as mages know them (then it goes on about why they can' t be full mages)<br /> and the it says &quot;some rare shapeshifters are able to learn certain paths of hedge magic. sphere's magic's poor cousin. however it's hardly common practice whenall''s said and done the shapeshifters gifts and rites are at least as potent if not more so only the most curious or completist of the changing breeds feel the need to learn such human wizardry<br /> <br /> this seems to imply that other splats who have innate powers should be able to use sorcery. after all they to have some &quot;power&quot; they can bend right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhh... no, not quite. I think you are somehow misreading that, or making an extrapolation that isn't implied by the citation, at all. Other books already cover the why's/how's of Hedge Magic relative to &quot;x&quot; splat (as cited by myself and Redford above): vampires can't use Mortal Hedge Magic because they aren't alive and no longer have the metaphysical connection to the appropriate mythic threads to employ said magics (though they may bastardize many of said principles and adopt them to their own Blood Magic); *some* few breed-changers can develop Hedge Magic, but generally most don't have the inclination, desire and/or talent to do so (plus, as cited, their own innate powers and/or ritualized magic usually suffices for them); Mages can't utilize static magic, proper, because they are metaphysically on a &quot;different playing field&quot;, once they Awaken; The Imbued are &quot;locked into&quot; their own metaphysical identity, and have their own assortment of potential hedge-powers/abilities, and therefore can't gain other Numinic powers; etc.... Being inherently mystical doesn't automatically mean that one can employ Sorcery -- in fact, in a number of cases, it actually precluded/eliminates the possibility, rather than allowing for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:57:04-08:00","id":362694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=360995#post360995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Changeling there might be some confusion due to terms used. Changeling can be a Sorcerer but that has nothing to do with Hedge Magic or mortal Sorcerers. Changeling Sorcerer is a Changeling with a considerable amount of Cantrips learned, I think, and this is straight out of memory ergo likely wrong, it was something on the line of having to have one set of Cantrips at level 5 and few others at level 4 to be considered Sorcerer the specifics escape me at the moment but they were rigorous demands that take a huge amount of exp to get if talking about a player.<br /> <br /> But no a Changeling is never gonna be using Hedge Magic they do not even have a merit for it unlike the Changers, the aforementioned Cat/Fox Magic 7-pts, or Vampires, in Wolves of the Sea (as mentioned by someone else) there is a 5pt Merits that allows them to have access to certain Paths of Hedge Magic but only certain Paths. So clearly it is meant to be something generally out of reach of Major Splats outside of expensive Merits that can grant access to them, the cost does not include the cost of the Path itself naturally thus keeping these to the truly dedicated few.<br /> <br /> Also WoD: Sorcerer as mentioned lays it out pretty straight saying that you loose your Hedge Magics should you become one of hte big splats but as an optional rule it gives you a list of what powers etc you might gain instead of your Path knowledge if and only if the ST is lenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you posted is essentially correct: there are Changeling [s]orcerers, but no Changeling [S]orcerers. Also, it bears clarifying that even with the bastardized Valdaermen magic, vis-a-vis &quot;Wolves of the Sea&quot;, that still isn't *mortal* Hedge Magic/Sorcery the einjenhar (sp?) are employing, but the vampire in question simply developing his own blood magic paths that mimic/simulate said mortal magic -- a trivial point, from a strict game-mechanic perspective, but a very important metaphysical point relative to the discussion at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T13:14:08-08:00","id":362829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=362694#post362694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you posted is essentially correct: there are Changeling [s]orcerers, but no Changeling [S]orcerers. Also, it bears clarifying that even with the bastardized Valdaermen magic, vis-a-vis &quot;Wolves of the Sea&quot;, that still isn't *mortal* Hedge Magic/Sorcery the einjenhar (sp?) are employing, but the vampire in question simply developing his own blood magic paths that mimic/simulate said mortal magic -- a trivial point, from a strict game-mechanic perspective, but a very important metaphysical point relative to the discussion at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>True on all accounts.<br /> <br /> I checked my sources and a Changeling sorcerer is one who has at the bare minimum mastered one Art, level 5, and Adept at a second one, level 4. But yeah Changelings cannot become Sorcerers in the wield Hedge Magic sort of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T03:42:09-08:00","id":363312,"title":"","content":"Technocratic Enlightened citizens could be slightly different to other sorcerers. A lot of the Technocratic paradigm rests on having the right gear, ie. magical items created by actual Technocrats. Therefore they may not need paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T05:21:58-08:00","id":363393,"title":"","content":"<br /> Not necessarily. CWoD Sorcery is not like Exalted's thaumaturgy, where any being with knowledge and magical fuel can make use of it. Not every splat or character in the CWoD is going to have the metaphysical underpinnings to use it. Just because a splat has a source of supernatural power, that does not guarantee that they can manipulate their power (like the Tremere did to obtain Blood Magic), or that their power is even compatible with Sorcery (such as with the Imbued a.k.a. &quot;Hunters&quot;).[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> so to sum it up: a)not every power source has &quot;loopholes&quot; and/or the power/correct power/potential that allow it to be bended to create their equivelant of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> b.in order to use static sorcery one must be either a human and have an avatar( after all gilguled can't be sorcerers) a sleeping one but still. or at the very least he has to be/have sth very similar such as a few breeds of fera and maybe the occasional werewolf who are part human anyway. a human body but nearly completely different soul and power(like changelings whose magic is the exact opposite ) does not suffice<br /> <br /> c.a vampire learng from a sorcerer would thus achieve nothing or at most with effort he could effectively develop blood magic that mimic'ssorcery's effects just like the tremere did","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 01-08-2015, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T10:38:16-08:00","id":364548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=363393#post363393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so to sum it up: a)not every power source has &quot;loopholes&quot; and/or the power/correct power/potential that allow it to be bended to create their equivelant of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> b.in order to use static sorcery one must be either a human and have an avatar( after all gilguled can't be sorcerers) a sleeping one but still. or at the very least he has to be/have sth very similar such as a few breeds of fera and maybe the occasional werewolf who are part human anyway. a human body but nearly completely different soul and power(like changelings whose magic is the exact opposite ) does not suffice<br /> <br /> c.a vampire learng from a sorcerer would thus achieve nothing or at most with effort he could effectively develop blood magic that mimic'ssorcery's effects just like the tremere did</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Of course, these are based on the rules for creating Player Characters and establishing the baseline of the setting. The Storyteller can (and sometimes should) make exceptions to the &quot;rules&quot; if it benefits their story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:21:54-08:00","id":1016276,"title":"","content":"I would do a little necromancy here but:<br /> <br /> Im about to start a changing breed (with mixed oriental and occidental breeds) with a kitsune monk / shinto shaman.<br /> I get my hands on a the merit to learn static magic (7pt cost) but Im in some questions.<br /> Frist , with how many points i have to spend on the path (Im going with mana manipulation and some of the spirit naming path that I dont remember now) ?<br /> Second: How much cost to gain new levels of this paths o how do you learn new paths? Only with mentors?<br /> Last: What traditions suits better for de concept that Im thinking for this character?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12760-mesen","name":"mesen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:04:02-08:00","id":1016354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mesen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=1016276#post1016276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would do a little necromancy here but:<br /> <br /> Im about to start a changing breed (with mixed oriental and occidental breeds) with a kitsune monk / shinto shaman.<br /> I get my hands on a the merit to learn static magic (7pt cost) but Im in some questions.<br /> Frist , with how many points i have to spend on the path (Im going with mana manipulation and some of the spirit naming path that I dont remember now) ?<br /> Second: How much cost to gain new levels of this paths o how do you learn new paths? Only with mentors?<br /> Last: What traditions suits better for de concept that Im thinking for this character?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>According to Sorcerer Revised (I don't feel like combing through all my books just to check other sources), each dot in a Path costs 7 freebie points at character creation. After char gen, it costs 7 XP for new Paths, and new rating * 7 to upgrade from there. It's an expensive habit, Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Learning Path knowledge can be done through a teacher, sure, although &quot;teacher&quot; in this case could include occult tomes or spirit mentors. A ghost of a shinto priest could teach them, as could a kami spirit (the Japanese naturae, not the capital-K Kami from W20) who wants to reestablish the proper ways of giving respect to the spirit world.<br /> <br /> For Traditions, either the Akashayana (Akashic Brotherhood) or Dreamspeakers would work very well in this regard. I would go with the Dreamspeakers, first because of Shintoism's animistic nature, and second because the Dreamspeakers have the least antagonistic relationship with the Changing Breeds. Moreover, as a Fera themself, your character would find themselves most at home talking to them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there are potential difficulties when learning from Mages. At least according to Dragons of the East, Kitsune have a nasty habit of capturing Mages and torturing them for the secrets to Sphere Magick. No idea how common that is, but it's bound to leave a bad impression among Mages about the were-foxes, assuming this is at all a common activity. It's not a deal breaker by any means - this could provide the basis for interesting story possibilities - but it does make such interactions awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:27:54-08:00","id":1016362,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to do old fashioned Sorcery, you need to look at Hedge Wizard, when Sorcerers were explicitly crossover. The only Shadow Folk who explicitly cannot learn Sorcery are Mages, Mummies, Risen, and Wraiths (though STs are given permission to forbid Shadow Folk Sorcerers if they do not want to bother). It really is not abusive to have Shadow Folk learn Sorcery though, as they are often better off learning their own powers, so it does not really give Shadow Folk any advantage (other than some flexibility) to learn Sorcery.<br /> <br /> In my own games, I have had a few players who played Shadow Folk who learned Sorcery. They would develop the 1st level and return to learning their own Gifts (there was no need to require a 7 point Merit). A Sorcery Path costs 77 XP to develop from 0 to 5. Garou can learn (Auspice, Breed, or Clan) two level 1 Gifts, two level 2 Gifts, two level 3 Gifts, two level 4 Gifts, and one level 5 Gift. So Garou can learn one Path of limited utility or nine Gifts with a wide range of utility. There really is no comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T04:19:22-08:00","id":1016487,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12760-mesen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12760\" data-vbnamecard=\"12760\">mesen</a> a Suggestion if I may... avoid the spirit dealings Sorceries as the Shapeshifter's rites and umbral capacity are vastly more powerful and cheaper to enact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:09:25-08:00","id":1016532,"title":"","content":"If a player wants to learn Sorcery, let them learn Sorcery, just be prepared to hear them whine when they find out that Sorcery is less effective that their Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:52:43-08:00","id":1017738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/359022-can-splats-learn-sorcery?p=1016362#post1016362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you want to do old fashioned Sorcery, you need to look at Hedge Wizard, when Sorcerers were explicitly crossover. The only Shadow Folk who explicitly cannot learn Sorcery are Mages, Mummies, Risen, and Wraiths (though STs are given permission to forbid Shadow Folk Sorcerers if they do not want to bother). It really is not abusive to have Shadow Folk learn Sorcery though, as they are often better off learning their own powers, so it does not really give Shadow Folk any advantage (other than some flexibility) to learn Sorcery.<br /> <br /> In my own games, I have had a few players who played Shadow Folk who learned Sorcery. They would develop the 1st level and return to learning their own Gifts (there was no need to require a 7 point Merit). A Sorcery Path costs 77 XP to develop from 0 to 5. Garou can learn (Auspice, Breed, or Clan) two level 1 Gifts, two level 2 Gifts, two level 3 Gifts, two level 4 Gifts, and one level 5 Gift. So Garou can learn one Path of limited utility or nine Gifts with a wide range of utility. There really is no comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont mind de xp cost , I just wanna a cool power that other cant have and that its out of the thinking of the fera. You know when &quot;the dancer cant know why I can had the true name of their banes s&quot; kind of power.<br /> Thx for the help, know I would have to create a master /history to justify a have a tome of master on this powers. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12760-mesen","name":"mesen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}